/*
Problem: Same Tree
Platform: LeetCode (LC 100)
Topic: Binary Tree / DFS / Recursion

---------------------------------------------------------

Approach:

Two binary trees are considered the same if:

1. They have the same structure.
2. Corresponding nodes have equal values.

This naturally suggests using recursion.

---------------------------------------------------------

Recursive Idea:

For every pair of nodes:

Case 1:

Both are NULL

Trees match at this position.

Return true.

--------------------------------

Case 2:

One is NULL and the other isn't

Structures differ.

Return false.

--------------------------------

Case 3:

Both exist

Check:

1. Current node values are equal.
2. Left subtrees are the same.
3. Right subtrees are the same.

Return true only if all three
conditions are true.

---------------------------------------------------------

Recursive Formula:

SameTree(p, q) =

(p->val == q->val)

AND

SameTree(p->left, q->left)

AND

SameTree(p->right, q->right)

---------------------------------------------------------

Example:

Tree 1:

      1
     / \
    2   3

Tree 2:

      1
     / \
    2   3

--------------------------------

Compare:

1 == 1 ✔

Compare left:

2 == 2 ✔

Both children NULL ✔

Compare right:

3 == 3 ✔

Result:

true

---------------------------------------------------------

Example 2:

Tree 1:

    1
   /
  2

Tree 2:

    1
     \
      2

At second level:

NULL vs Node(2)

Return false.

---------------------------------------------------------

Why It Works?

Every recursive call compares
the corresponding nodes.

If any value or structure differs,
false immediately propagates upward.

---------------------------------------------------------

Time Complexity:

O(n)

Every node is visited once.

---------------------------------------------------------

Space Complexity:

O(h)

h = height of tree

Recursive call stack.

Worst case:

O(n)

Best (balanced tree):

O(log n)

---------------------------------------------------------
*/

class Solution {
public:
    bool isSameTree(TreeNode* p, TreeNode* q) {

        // If one or both nodes are NULL
        if (p == NULL || q == NULL)
            return p == q;

        // Compare left subtrees
        bool isLeftSame =
            isSameTree(p->left, q->left);

        // Compare right subtrees
        bool isRightSame =
            isSameTree(p->right, q->right);

        // Current nodes must also match
        return isLeftSame &&
               isRightSame &&
               p->val == q->val;
    }
};
